#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186063953 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "89f65f58-bd3d-5c3f-b9e0-462d74d75b59" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Second Order Derivatives"}] :question/id #uuid "0bc72287-b782-5add-89ef-f2a465573ab0" :question/is-example true :question/math-academy-id "e-3653" :question/problem "Find $f''(x)$ for $f(x) = 2x^3 + \\dfrac 1 x$." :question/worked-solution "Computing the first derivative, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf^{′}(x) &= (2x^{3} + \\frac{1}{x})^{′} \\\\\n&= (2x^{3} + x^{-1})^{′} \\\\\n&= 2(3)x^{2} - x^{-2} \\\\\n&= 6x^{2} - x^{-2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the second derivative, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf^{″}(x) &= (6x^{2} - x^{-2})^{′} \\\\\n&= 6(2)x - (-2)x^{-3} \\\\\n&= 12x + 2x^{-3}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186063954 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6afb4058-908a-5983-9c1e-78ee3fbadf44" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Second Order Derivatives Using Leibnitz Notation"}] :question/id #uuid "b092bc79-d369-5ff0-a6bb-5fc059699275" :question/is-example true :question/math-academy-id "e-3654" :question/problem "Calculate $\\dfrac {\\textrm d^2 y}{\\textrm d x^2}$ for $y = 3 x^4 + 5x+ \\sqrt x$." :question/worked-solution "Computing the first derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{dy}{dx} &= \\frac{d}{dx}(3x^{4} + 5x + \\sqrt{x}) \\\\\n&= \\frac{d}{dx}(3x^{4} + 5x + x^{1/2}) \\\\\n&= 3(4)x^{3} + 5 + \\frac{1}{2}x^{-1/2} \\\\\n&= 12x^{3} + 5 + \\frac{1}{2}x^{-1/2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the second derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{d^{2}y}{dx^{2}} &= \\frac{d}{dx}(12x^{3} + 5 + \\frac{1}{2}x^{-1/2}) \\\\\n&= 12(3)x^{2} + 0 + \\frac{1}{2}(-\\frac{1}{2})x^{-3/2} \\\\\n&= 36x^{2} - \\frac{1}{4}x^{-3/2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186063955 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "322168bb-52e3-5352-a2e3-c5bdbf2bc13e" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Higher Order Derivatives"}] :question/id #uuid "627f1ef4-64a8-5764-89c7-cb4e31009dbe" :question/is-example true :question/math-academy-id "e-3655" :question/problem "Given $y = \\dfrac {3 x^2 + x - 1} x$, find $\\dfrac {\\textrm d^{3} y} {\\textrm d x^3}$." :question/worked-solution "First, notice that we can rewrite the function as the sum of powers of $x$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny &= \\frac{3x^{2} + x - 1}{x} \\\\\n&= \\frac{3x^{2}}{x} + \\frac{x}{x} - \\frac{1}{x} \\\\\n&= 3x + 1 - x^{-1}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the first derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{dy}{dx} &= \\frac{d}{dx}(3x + 1 - x^{-1}) \\\\\n&= 3 + 0 - (-1)x^{-2} \\\\\n&= 3 + x^{-2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the second derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{d^{2}y}{dx^{2}} &= \\frac{d}{dx}(3 + x^{-2}) \\\\\n&= 0 + (-2)x^{-3} \\\\\n&=-2x^{-3}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, computing the third derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{d^{3}y}{dx^{3}} &= \\frac{d}{dx}(-2x^{-3}) \\\\\n&=-2(-3)x^{-4} \\\\\n&= 6x^{-4}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186245839 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6afb4058-908a-5983-9c1e-78ee3fbadf44" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Second Order Derivatives Using Leibnitz Notation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f0fc0225-3148-53f2-bae4-62d9b9c78857" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}-\\frac{1}{{x}^{4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245841} {:answer/id #uuid "bfd8b1df-cb57-5b27-846d-b7b2f05b7806" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{x}^{4}}-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245842} {:answer/id #uuid "852caae1-5fa1-571f-bed1-5f33329f1373" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2{x}^{4}}+\\frac{1}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245843} {:answer/id #uuid "216681df-7b18-5a5e-8da1-488e2cb7fe70" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}-\\frac{1}{2{x}^{4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245844} {:answer/id #uuid "c527c1a7-7b0c-5f8c-b01b-0d4afcbdfc1d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3{x}^{3}}-\\frac{2}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245845}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bfd8b1df-cb57-5b27-846d-b7b2f05b7806" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{x}^{4}}-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245842} :answer-field/id #uuid "32a5db2b-2744-535d-bca9-60f41d0e6c1c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245840}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9a5035fe-0639-5869-866e-1f7ac70119d9" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-104191" :question/problem "Calculate $\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}$ for $y=ln⁡x+\\frac{1}{6{x}^{2}}.$" :question/worked-solution "Computing the first derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(ln⁡x+\\frac{1}{6{x}^{2}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(ln⁡x+\\frac{1}{6}{x}^{-2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{x}+\\frac{1}{6}\\cdot (-2){x}^{-2-1} \\\\  & ={x}^{-1}-\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{-3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the second derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{-1}-\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{-3}) \\\\  & =(-1){x}^{-1-1}-\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot (-3){x}^{-3-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{x}^{4}}-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186245846 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6afb4058-908a-5983-9c1e-78ee3fbadf44" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Second Order Derivatives Using Leibnitz Notation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03cb8d3f-a34a-52f7-be5d-6543a24c1212" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{{x}^{5}}}+cos⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245848} {:answer/id #uuid "25d730ce-6aaa-5ad4-995b-53120e4b8cbe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\sqrt{{x}^{5}}-2cos⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245849} {:answer/id #uuid "4cd6e750-33b6-5b43-a57f-45206a822ab3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{{x}^{5}}-sin⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245850} {:answer/id #uuid "6f4a9bd0-3447-5c93-9307-ef6ab4a221d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3\\sqrt{{x}^{5}}}+2sin⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245851} {:answer/id #uuid "2df03b6e-2dc8-518a-8f7d-2e7055aaee3b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{{x}^{5}}}-2sin⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245852}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2df03b6e-2dc8-518a-8f7d-2e7055aaee3b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{{x}^{5}}}-2sin⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245852} :answer-field/id #uuid "6a49fb81-bbb4-5f7c-8a0c-407153c0252f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245847}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e0bfdda6-c7ad-5a9e-b68f-6ae0e04aa7b0" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-104192" :question/problem "Calculate $\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}$ for $y=\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{x}}+2sin⁡x.$" :question/worked-solution "Computing the first derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{x}}+2sin⁡x) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(4{x}^{-1/2}+2sin⁡x) \\\\  & =4(-\\frac{1}{2}){x}^{-1/2-1}+2cos⁡x \\\\  & =-2{x}^{-3/2}+2cos⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the second derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-2{x}^{-3/2}+2cos⁡x) \\\\  & =-2(-\\frac{3}{2}){x}^{-3/2-1}-2sin⁡x \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{{x}^{5}}}-2sin⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186245853 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "89f65f58-bd3d-5c3f-b9e0-462d74d75b59" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Second Order Derivatives"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "55ea16ee-4963-5713-b5c0-f4eb31b25243" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{5}}}+10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245855} {:answer/id #uuid "1637c207-be3b-5713-9c7f-2c8de558a855" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{5}}}+10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245856} {:answer/id #uuid "3deb103e-44e9-5261-894a-9c44386bd6da" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{3}}}+10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245857} {:answer/id #uuid "aa955f6e-beed-5e45-907f-41c258228ba2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{3}}}-10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245858} {:answer/id #uuid "d101fa51-9bf7-514a-8aa8-e100da4c85f4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24{x}^{2}-24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245859}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3deb103e-44e9-5261-894a-9c44386bd6da" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{3}}}+10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245857} :answer-field/id #uuid "09cf53ec-6c37-5dde-870d-48fc54ee3e3b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245854}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "dcea6f8f-2ced-53e3-b506-29a6149315bf" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-10883" :question/problem "Find ${f}^{″}(x)$ for $f(x)=4\\sqrt{x}+5{x}^{2}+x.$" :question/worked-solution "Computing the first derivative, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={(4\\sqrt{x}+5{x}^{2}+x)}^{′} \\\\  & ={(4{x}^{1/2}+5{x}^{2}+x)}^{′} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 4{x}^{-1/2}+2\\cdot 5x+1 \\\\  & =2{x}^{-1/2}+10x+1\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the second derivative, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(x) & ={(2{x}^{-1/2}+10x+1)}^{′} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 2{x}^{-3/2}+10+0 \\\\  & =-{x}^{-3/2}+10 \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{3}}}+10.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186245860 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6afb4058-908a-5983-9c1e-78ee3fbadf44" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Second Order Derivatives Using Leibnitz Notation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "af0ec77a-bca4-5677-bbb4-3808634f61b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "30{x}^{3}+24x-20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245862} {:answer/id #uuid "83b5c389-6322-5277-b0e9-c83db03edfbc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "60{x}^{3}+48x-20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245863} {:answer/id #uuid "fe9e79e9-0c5e-5884-aed5-1b7c442fa3ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "60{x}^{3}+24x-22" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245864} {:answer/id #uuid "2c3f0363-7636-5707-b4b4-c32bfce441d0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "60{x}^{3}-24x-20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245865} {:answer/id #uuid "a3bdd116-956e-5363-bc41-a607d629264a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "60{x}^{3}+24x-20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245866}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a3bdd116-956e-5363-bc41-a607d629264a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "60{x}^{3}+24x-20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245866} :answer-field/id #uuid "3ee4c3f3-dcb0-5251-a475-8e2e06b41c4f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245861}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c9616344-ca96-5e7c-a4c8-e4600a490221" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-10884" :question/problem "Calculate $\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}$ for $y=3{x}^{5}+4{x}^{3}-10{x}^{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "Computing the first derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3{x}^{5}+4{x}^{3}-10{x}^{2}) \\\\  & =5\\cdot 3{x}^{4}+3\\cdot 4{x}^{2}-2\\cdot 10x \\\\  & =15{x}^{4}+12{x}^{2}-20x\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the second derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(15{x}^{4}+12{x}^{2}-20x) \\\\  & =15\\cdot 4{x}^{3}+2\\cdot 12x-20 \\\\  & =60{x}^{3}+24x-20.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186245867 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "89f65f58-bd3d-5c3f-b9e0-462d74d75b59" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Second Order Derivatives"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c40357b2-da5e-56c5-9428-c87c9a970945" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245869} {:answer/id #uuid "1f4808c8-a4bb-5bbd-91d8-15f73ab306a8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245870} {:answer/id #uuid "9a044331-b5ff-513d-a64f-ebfaea1ae8f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "21" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245871} {:answer/id #uuid "1f6b4f29-8791-534f-9d1c-da01ac026d49" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245872} {:answer/id #uuid "619c1bd2-c3e1-5cd8-9a9c-285ecf1ef538" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-21" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245873}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c40357b2-da5e-56c5-9428-c87c9a970945" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245869} :answer-field/id #uuid "a31a1465-68c2-5dc5-8f76-ad8c60dd84c0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245868}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f7d53911-e22c-50ee-9d76-06a1ee070f97" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-10892" :question/problem "Find ${f}^{″}(-2)$ if $f(x)=2{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}-7.$" :question/worked-solution "Computing the first derivative, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={(2{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}-7)}^{′} &  \\\\  & =3\\cdot 2{x}^{2}+2\\cdot 4x-0 \\\\  & =6{x}^{2}+8x\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the second derivative, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(x) & ={(6{x}^{2}+8x)}^{′} \\\\  & =2\\cdot 6x+8 \\\\  & =12x+8\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, evaluating the second derivative at $x=-2$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(-2) & =12(-2)+8 \\\\  & =-24+8 \\\\  & =-16.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186245874 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "89f65f58-bd3d-5c3f-b9e0-462d74d75b59" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Second Order Derivatives"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c9be8058-50c7-541c-a65b-a707ad9f15a9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "35{x}^{4}+20{x}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245876} {:answer/id #uuid "e2a62236-74ba-58e4-86a6-15e323925af5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "30{x}^{4}+20{x}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245877} {:answer/id #uuid "33fae81b-3ea6-5f1b-94e6-1ba75b81155a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "30{x}^{5}+20{x}^{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245878} {:answer/id #uuid "48d59405-d5ad-5428-8fc4-c6d943e2a444" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "40{x}^{3}+30{x}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245879} {:answer/id #uuid "8783571c-6c5a-563d-8d93-a5fd347131e9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "30{x}^{4}+25{x}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245880}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e2a62236-74ba-58e4-86a6-15e323925af5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "30{x}^{4}+20{x}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245877} :answer-field/id #uuid "c3ea300c-223c-555c-8f0b-a82e6bca6a72" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245875}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f57e3668-6559-58e3-8b4a-23bfd386a16c" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-10902" :question/problem "Find ${f}^{″}(x)$ for $f(x)={x}^{6}+{x}^{5}.$" :question/worked-solution "Computing the first derivative, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={({x}^{6}+{x}^{5})}^{′} \\\\  & =6\\cdot {x}^{5}+5\\cdot {x}^{4} \\\\  & =6{x}^{5}+5{x}^{4}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the second derivative, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(x) & ={(6{x}^{5}+5{x}^{4})}^{′} \\\\  & =5\\cdot 6{x}^{4}+4\\cdot 5{x}^{3} \\\\  & =30{x}^{4}+20{x}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064386 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6afb4058-908a-5983-9c1e-78ee3fbadf44" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Second Order Derivatives Using Leibnitz Notation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f77246d2-bf58-519a-bbaf-ee09cdb86d59" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "60x^{2} + 8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061001} {:answer/id #uuid "fb658a6f-2c8e-5660-be3f-55653f958ed8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "60x^{2} + 12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061002} {:answer/id #uuid "28e3a2fd-855c-5325-beb9-f4fdb154f5ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "60x^{2} + 8x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061003} {:answer/id #uuid "3ba93afd-1f36-569a-ad56-214b680c4d32" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "60x^{3} + 8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061004} {:answer/id #uuid "5c95949e-ebd7-570e-b81b-4f6841c44dfb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "30x^{2} + 8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061005}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f77246d2-bf58-519a-bbaf-ee09cdb86d59" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "60x^{2} + 8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061001} :answer-field/id #uuid "cb8a5c74-2a77-50c7-9c52-1acb0dde8448" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061000}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b7a8a2be-ff9a-5f4a-96bd-e383a3bb4443" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-10903" :question/problem "Calculate $\\frac{d^{2}y}{dx^{2}}$ for $y = 5x^{4} + 4x^{2}$." :question/worked-solution "Computing the first derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(5{x}^{4}+4{x}^{2}) \\\\  & =4\\cdot 5{x}^{3}+2\\cdot 4x \\\\  & =20{x}^{3}+8x\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the second derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(20{x}^{3}+8x) \\\\  & =3\\cdot 20{x}^{2}+8 \\\\  & =60{x}^{2}+8.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064613 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "322168bb-52e3-5352-a2e3-c5bdbf2bc13e" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Higher Order Derivatives"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "14cfdc6e-08b0-5dd1-91e2-5befc2d808ca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{6}{x^{4}} + 6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186062190} {:answer/id #uuid "166dd873-9e9e-57f0-91f1-f6e766ab0fd7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{6}{x^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186062191} {:answer/id #uuid "3e457b76-2abf-5cce-8555-059d2916592c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{6}{x^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186062192} {:answer/id #uuid "55122213-8778-56f1-b516-e8b87df6b11a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{18}{x^{4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186062193} {:answer/id #uuid "5f3f9373-66b6-5dea-adf6-76f1316c9d63" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{18}{x^{4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186062194}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5f3f9373-66b6-5dea-adf6-76f1316c9d63" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{18}{x^{4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186062194} :answer-field/id #uuid "d4781585-d27a-595a-aabb-decf044a4499" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186062189}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b83e7d12-8550-5720-b6a4-35cd583e538f" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-28546" :question/problem "Given $h(x) = 3x^{2} - 5x + \\frac{3}{x}$, find $h^{‴}(x)$." :question/worked-solution "First, notice that we can rewrite the function as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}h(x) & =3{x}^{2}-5x+\\frac{3}{x} \\\\  & =3{x}^{2}-5x+3{x}^{-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the first derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{h}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3{x}^{2}-5x+3{x}^{-1}) \\\\  & =6x-5-3{x}^{-2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the second derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{h}^{″}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(6x-5-3{x}^{-2}) \\\\  & =6+6{x}^{-3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, computing the third derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{h}^{‴}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(6+6{x}^{-3}) \\\\  & =-18{x}^{-4} \\\\  & =-\\frac{18}{{x}^{4}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186245881 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "89f65f58-bd3d-5c3f-b9e0-462d74d75b59" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Second Order Derivatives"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1909bd0d-7c92-554a-85e1-6ffc1df4f17b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "60" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245883} {:answer/id #uuid "7ee1662d-dea8-5d01-89c3-48c180a6f121" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245884} {:answer/id #uuid "74f45517-793a-55c0-992b-ada83f6515b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "120" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245885} {:answer/id #uuid "3f7564e8-b5bc-549b-bb71-af16e4f99e5f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "45" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245886} {:answer/id #uuid "d0eac07d-22da-5e4a-bbeb-ac208ac00a6b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "75" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245887}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7ee1662d-dea8-5d01-89c3-48c180a6f121" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245884} :answer-field/id #uuid "9c7844d1-132c-5cc2-9c73-53aa1ae43ba0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245882}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "2228ba5b-177e-5571-a1af-ea713584740f" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-28556" :question/problem "Find ${g}^{″}(4)$ if $g(x)=4{x}^{2}\\sqrt{x}-2x+7.$" :question/worked-solution "Computing the first derivative, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(x) & ={(4{x}^{2}\\sqrt{x}-2x+7)}^{′} \\\\  & ={(4{x}^{5/2}-2x+7)}^{′} \\\\  & =4(\\frac{5}{2}){x}^{3/2}-2+0 \\\\  & =10{x}^{3/2}-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the second derivative, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{″}(x) & ={(10{x}^{3/2}-2)}^{′} \\\\  & =10(\\frac{3}{2}){x}^{1/2}-0 \\\\  & =15{x}^{1/2} \\\\  & =15\\sqrt{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, evaluating the second derivative at $x=4$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{″}(4) & =15\\sqrt{4} \\\\  & =15(2) \\\\  & =30.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186245888 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "89f65f58-bd3d-5c3f-b9e0-462d74d75b59" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Second Order Derivatives"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "56922837-6471-5037-b596-ee75655a6e1c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245890}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "56922837-6471-5037-b596-ee75655a6e1c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245890} :answer-field/id #uuid "4f626f2e-3d66-5e46-8c01-28c22c432e35" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245889}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "89d72708-85f3-50d8-be7c-f6b79aaead58" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-342851" :question/problem "Find ${g}^{″}(1)$ if $g(x)=-{x}^{3}+4x\\sqrt{x}.$\n\n${g}^{″}(1)=$ \n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Computing the first derivative, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(x) & ={(-{x}^{3}+4x\\sqrt{x})}^{′} \\\\  & ={(-{x}^{3}+4{x}^{3/2})}^{′} \\\\  & =3(-{x}^{2})+\\frac{3}{2}(4{x}^{1/2}) \\\\  & =-3{x}^{2}+6{x}^{1/2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the second derivative, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{″}(x) & ={(-3{x}^{2}+6{x}^{1/2})}^{′} \\\\  & =2(-3x)+\\frac{1}{2}(6{x}^{-1/2}) \\\\  & =-6x+3{x}^{-1/2} \\\\  & =-6x+\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{x}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, evaluating the second derivative at $x=1$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{″}(1) & =-6(1)+\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{1}} \\\\  & =-6+3 \\\\  & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186245891 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6afb4058-908a-5983-9c1e-78ee3fbadf44" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Second Order Derivatives Using Leibnitz Notation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fa0199b9-8144-5c89-a178-de5cedf0971b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6-8x^{-3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245893}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fa0199b9-8144-5c89-a178-de5cedf0971b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6-8x^{-3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245893} :answer-field/id #uuid "dcd7d2df-ba0e-51af-9f41-bdfc00719585" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245892}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b685d3a8-eab1-551d-a03b-58f7aef8f487" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-342877" :question/problem "Calculate $\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}$ for $y=\\frac{6{x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}-8}{2x}.$\n\n$\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}=$ \n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Computing the first derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{6{x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}-8}{2x}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3{x}^{2}+x-4{x}^{-1}) \\\\  & =6x+1+(-1)(-4{x}^{-2}) \\\\  & =6x+1+4{x}^{-2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the second derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(6x+1+4{x}^{-2}) \\\\  & =6+0+(-2)(4{x}^{-3}) \\\\  & =6-\\frac{8}{{x}^{3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186245894 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "322168bb-52e3-5352-a2e3-c5bdbf2bc13e" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Higher Order Derivatives"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ed41d023-2a82-552f-b332-6d20dbb20ad7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "120x^2-18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245896}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ed41d023-2a82-552f-b332-6d20dbb20ad7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "120x^2-18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245896} :answer-field/id #uuid "8b905a51-b17c-5ed0-9b38-fc78eb0b0847" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245895}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6706cc48-5043-57c9-8414-fca036ac3a21" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-343075" :question/problem "Given $g(x)=2{x}^{5}-3{x}^{3},$ we have\n\n${g}^{‴}(x)=$ \n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Computing the first derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2{x}^{5}-3{x}^{3}) \\\\  & =10{x}^{4}-9{x}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the second derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{″}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(10{x}^{4}-9{x}^{2}) \\\\  & =40{x}^{3}-18x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, computing the third derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{‴}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(40{x}^{3}-18x) \\\\  & =120{x}^{2}-18.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186245897 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "322168bb-52e3-5352-a2e3-c5bdbf2bc13e" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Higher Order Derivatives"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "94d696fe-4b2d-55cf-9ff1-99055f24ebe2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}-\\frac{3}{2}x^{-4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245899}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "94d696fe-4b2d-55cf-9ff1-99055f24ebe2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}-\\frac{3}{2}x^{-4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245899} :answer-field/id #uuid "b1f49f14-a171-531c-b121-6fb15a980a34" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245898}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "78e7de72-357a-5c97-92cd-d27b4d4dfb54" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-343086" :question/problem "Given $f(x)=\\frac{{x}^{5}-{x}^{2}+x}{4{x}^{2}},$ we have\n\n${f}^{‴}(x)=$ \n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "First, notice that we can rewrite the function as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\frac{{x}^{5}-{x}^{2}+x}{4{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{3}}{4}-\\frac{1}{4}+\\frac{1}{4x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the first derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{{x}^{3}}{4}-\\frac{1}{4}+\\frac{1}{4x}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{{x}^{3}}{4}-\\frac{1}{4}+\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{-1}) \\\\  & =\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{4}-\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{-2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the second derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{4}-\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{-2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{3x}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{-3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, computing the third derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{‴}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{3x}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{-3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}-\\frac{3}{2}{x}^{-4} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}-\\frac{3}{2{x}^{4}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186245900 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "322168bb-52e3-5352-a2e3-c5bdbf2bc13e" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Higher Order Derivatives"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b772a37-e8b0-5a6e-961d-27948ec23264" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4x^{-3}+24x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245902} {:answer/id #uuid "d8561762-eb0e-5d03-b2d8-9f218eca293b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4x^{-3}+24x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245903}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d8561762-eb0e-5d03-b2d8-9f218eca293b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4x^{-3}+24x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245903} :answer-field/id #uuid "b4720fdb-7da3-5e1b-bfd6-d997cd609cd5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245901}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7891f6b5-04df-57d0-aa50-3e1688cc9d59" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-343114" :question/problem "Given $f(x)=2ln⁡x+{x}^{4},$ we have\n\n${f}^{‴}(x)=$ \n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Computing the first derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2ln⁡x+{x}^{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{x}+4{x}^{3} \\\\  & =2{x}^{-1}+4{x}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the second derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2{x}^{-1}+4{x}^{3}) \\\\  & =-2{x}^{-2}+12{x}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, computing the third derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{‴}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-2{x}^{-2}+12{x}^{2}) \\\\  & =4{x}^{-3}+24x \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{{x}^{3}}+24x.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186245904 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "322168bb-52e3-5352-a2e3-c5bdbf2bc13e" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Higher Order Derivatives"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cbb1dcd8-1924-5ce0-82d7-1f6bc0ea771f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sin(x)+e^x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245906} {:answer/id #uuid "90aa6bcf-291a-53f4-9bc3-7e22a1cd4f06" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sin(x)-e^x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245907}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "90aa6bcf-291a-53f4-9bc3-7e22a1cd4f06" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sin(x)-e^x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245907} :answer-field/id #uuid "0fb27c2f-a019-539a-ab72-a8ed081a927e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245905}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "b4d6e47e-90c0-5c0e-a6ae-7bd34acadde5" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-343120" :question/problem "Find ${g}^{(4)}(x)$ for $g(x)=sin⁡x-{e}^{x}.$\n\n${g}^{(4)}(x)=$ \n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Computing the first derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(sin⁡x-{e}^{x}) \\\\  & =cos⁡x-{e}^{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the second derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{″}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(cos⁡x-{e}^{x}) \\\\  & =-sin⁡x-{e}^{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the third derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{‴}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-sin⁡x-{e}^{x}) \\\\  & =-cos⁡x-{e}^{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, computing the fourth derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{(4)}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-cos⁡x-{e}^{x}) \\\\  & =sin⁡x-{e}^{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
